  m_Name: EarthInfo
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CelestialBodyInfo
  bodyName: Earth
  classification: Terrestrial Planet
  positionFromSun: 3rd Planet
  overview: Earth is the third planet from the Sun and the only known astronomical
    body to support life. Approximately 71% of its surface is covered by water. Earth
    has a nitrogen-oxygen atmosphere, a global magnetic field, and one natural moon.
  keyCharacteristics: '- Only known planet to support life.

    - Approximately
    71% of its surface is covered by water.

    - Has an active plate tectonic
    system.

    - Possesses a global magnetic field.

    - Has one natural satellite,
    the Moon.'
  meanRadiusKm: 6371
  meanDiameterKm: 12742
  massKg: 5.9722e+24
  meanDensityGcm3: 5.513
  surfaceGravityMs2: 9.82
  escapeVelocityKms: 11.186
  semiMajorAxisAU: 1.00000011
  orbitalPeriodDays: 365.256
  orbitalEccentricity: 0.01671022
  orbitalInclinationDeg: 0.00005
  perihelionAU: 0.9833
  aphelionAU: 1.0167
  meanOrbitalVelocityKms: 29.78
  siderealRotationPeriodDays: 0.9972708
  lengthOfDayHours: 24
  axialTiltDeg: 23.44
  atmosphericComposition: '78.08% Nitrogen (N2)

    20.95% Oxygen (O2)

    0.93%
    Argon (Ar)

    Approximately 0.04% Carbon Dioxide (CO2)

    Variable water
    vapour, typically around 1%.

    Other trace gases.'
  atmosphericPressureBar: 1.014
  minimumTemperatureC: 0
  meanTemperatureC: 15
  maximumTemperatureC: 20
  moonCount: 1
  notableMoons:
  - Moon
  internalStructure: 'Earth has a differentiated internal structure consisting of:

    -
    Crust: Thin, solid outer layer.

    - Mantle: Thick rocky layer with slow convection.

    -
    Outer Core: Liquid iron and nickel.

    - Inner Core: Solid iron-rich central
    region.'
  surfaceAndRings: 'Approximately 71% of Earth''s surface is covered by water.

    The
    remaining surface consists primarily of continents and islands.

    Earth has
    no planetary ring system.

    Its surface is shaped by plate tectonics, volcanism,

    erosion
    and impact processes.'
  magneticField: 'Earth has a global magnetic field generated primarily

    by
    the movement of electrically conducting liquid iron

    in its outer core.
    The magnetosphere interacts with

    the solar wind and helps protect the atmosphere.'
